1. King James Version text (1769 standard text)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Source: "King James Version + Apocrypha" (eng-kjv), the standardized text of
1769, courtesy of the CrossWire Bible Society and eBible.org
https://ebible.org/find/details.php?id=eng-kjv
License: Public Domain (outside the United Kingdom, where the King James
Version is subject to Crown letters patent)

The files under old_testament/ and new_testament/ contain the 66 canonical
books only, one verse per line. The italic markers for supplied words and the
paragraph marks were removed, and Psalm superscriptions are stored as verse 0.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Original language texts and lexicons (STEP Bible)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Datasets: TAHOT, TAGNT, TBESH, TBESG
Source: STEP Bible (https://www.STEPBible.org/)
Repository: https://github.com/STEPBible/STEPBible-Data
License: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Credit: STEP Bible (www.STEPBible.org). Data created initially by Tyndale
House Cambridge, now curated by STEP Bible.

These files are included under data/ (TAHOT_*.txt, TAGNT_*.txt, TBESH.txt,
TBESG.txt). They have not been modified from the upstream STEP Bible texts
beyond filename normalization for packaging.

When loading, the app reads these files as follows (the files themselves are
unchanged): words are keyed to KJV versification; Greek words follow the
Textus Receptus behind the KJV (TR readings from the variants column replace
differing words, and words absent from the TR are omitted); Hebrew words
reconstructed from the LXX ("X") and empty Ketiv placeholders are omitted.

